  "description": "Welcome to 32 Georges Quay Apartments – a spacious 4th floor residence set to the front of this highly sought-after development, offering bright interiors and breathtaking water views over the River Liffey.\r\n\r\nWell presented with a lovely bright outlook this contemporary apartment is likely to appeal to a wide audience. Internally the accommodation comprises an entrance hall, an open plan living / dining room, a separate kitchen, master bedroom and a main bathroom. Parking in not included. \r\n\r\nOnly a short walk from Trinity College, Grafton Street and The IFSC, the location of this apartment is superb with the Silicon Docks area also close by - ideal for employees of Facebook, Google, Airbnb and Accenture. Several prominent accountancy and law practices are also situated nearby at Grand Canal Dock. Immediately adjacent are local shops, a range of cafes, bars and restaurants. The property is also well served by public transport with the LUAS and Dart and a variety of bus routes all within a short walk.\r\n\r\nThis is a superb opportunity for a discerning purchaser to acquire a prime city centre apartment.\n\nEntrance Hall: Wood floor, wall mounted shelf with fitted mirror over, walk-in hot-press. Intercom to hall door.\n\nLiving Room: Wood floor, mock fireplace with timber mantlepiece and brick surround, stunning water view overlooking the River Liffey.\n\nKitchen: Tiled floor, extensive range of floor and eye level kitchen units with tiled splash back. Beko under counter fridge with cooler box, built-in Zanussi oven with 4 ring hob over and extractor hood, single drainer stainless steel sink and Hotpoint washer/dryer.\n\nMaster Bedroom: Spacious double bedroom with wood floor and built in wardrobes. Stunning water view overlooking the River Liffey.\n\nBathroom: Tiled floor, bath with shower attachment, pedestal w.h.b. with fitted mirror over and W/C.\n\nService Charge: €1,515 per year",
  "features": [
    "One-bedroom 4th floor apartment",
